# Security Rules

- Authorization is server-side.
- UI hiding is not access control.
- Validate all writes.
- Least privilege.
- MFA privileged internal roles.
- No secrets in source/public/admin responses.
- Sensitive source data never enters public API, Search, analytics, logs or client bundles.
- Audit privileged mutations.
- Validate file type/size.
- Use migrations.
- Test direct API attempts by lower-privilege roles.
- Deactivation revokes sessions while preserving authorship/history.
